      <description>Like Europe, California bet on a rapid transition away from fossil fuels. Germany went as far as banning nuclear energy. Years of regulations have left them with depleted supplies of energy, and the war in Iran has highlighted how vulnerable it is to supply shocks. Unfortunately, the impacts will be felt across the whole country.</description>
